text:
emma: opened PR to harmonize tool-calling examples across the structured-output and migration guides: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/489

leo: nice. quick asks: 1) show a validator-friendly JSON Schema, 2) include both object and positional-arg examples, 3) note backward-compat mapping from function_call.

priya: agreed. also found a handful of docs that use `tool_name` instead of `tool` 1 places. PR should normalize to `tool` and call out the rename.

emma: working on a compact schema and two parsing snippets. pasting minimal schema (copyable):```json
{
  "type":"object",
  "properties":{
    "tool":{"type":"string"},
    "args":{"oneOf":[{"type":"object"},{"type":"array"}]},
    "confidence":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1}
  },
  "required":["tool","args"],
  "additionalProperties":false
}
```

leo: perfect. for examples, add a concrete `url_fetch` schema showing required `url` property so users can validate quickly.

priya: and a short JS parse pattern so front-end devs know how to safely handle output. e.g.:```js
const resp = await client.generate(...);
const parsed = JSON.parse(resp.output);
const {tool, args} = parsed;
if (tool === 'url_fetch') { await fetch(args.url); }
```

emma: adding a small compatibility note: "If you used `function_call.name`/`arguments`, map to `tool`/`args`. Do not assume `confidence` is calibrated." will link to /guides/evals.

docs-bot: CI: docs lint + snippet-check passed for PR #489  4 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-) :white_check_mark:

leo: one more nit: add `additionalProperties: false` to the example schemas so validators catch typos.

emma: done. i'll push final commit and ask for a quick review; target merge T+1 business day. thanks! :rocket:
